# Verify edited lines (and neighbors)

After any file edit - especially Windows / PowerShell / ExternalShell patches - do **not** trust exit codes alone.

## Required check

Re-read the **edited line(s) plus a few surrounding lines** and look for:

- Literal escape junk: `` `r`n ``, `` `n ``, `\r\n` written as text, doubled backslashes in imports
- Broken imports / quotes / template strings
- Truncated or merged lines
- Accidental BOM / mojibake / wrong line endings that corrupt syntax
- Partial replacements that left both old and new text on one line

## If anything looks wrong

Fix it immediately in the same turn before continuing other work or telling the user it is done.
